{"schemaVersion":1,"slug":"3sum","title":"3Sum","pattern":"Two Pointers","difficulty":"Medium","leetcode":15,"prompt":"Find every distinct triple in the array that sums to zero. Two triples with the same three values count as one, whatever their positions.","examples":[{"input":"nums = [-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]","output":"[[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]","why":"Both triples sum to zero; the duplicate -1 does not create a third."},{"input":"nums = [0,1,1]","output":"[]","why":"No triple reaches zero."}],"constraints":["3 <= len(nums) <= 3000","No duplicate triples in the answer"],"approaches":[{"id":"brute-force","label":"Every triple","complexity":{"time":"O(n\u00b3)","space":"O(n)"},"viz":{"ordered":"array","i":"pointer:ordered","j":"pointer:ordered","k":"pointer:ordered"},"layout":{},"source":["def every_triple(nums):","    ordered = sorted(nums)","    out = []","    seen = {}","    for i in range(len(ordered) - 2):","        for j in range(i + 1, len(ordered) - 1):","            for k in range(j + 1, len(ordered)):","                if ordered[i] + ordered[j] + ordered[k] == 0:","                    key = str(ordered[i]) + \",\" + str(ordered[j]) + \",\" + str(ordered[k])","                    if key not in seen:","                        seen[key] = True","                        out.append([ordered[i], ordered[j], ordered[k]])","    return out"],"variants":[{"id":"typical","label":"Two triples","note":null,"result":[[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]],"steps":[{"line":0,"ops":[["set",["nums"],[-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]]],"note":null},{"line":1,"ops":[["set",["ordered"],[-4,-1,-1,0,1,2]]],"note":"values sit together, and each triple comes out in a canonical order."},{"line":2,"ops":[["set",["out"],[]]],"note":null},{"line":3,"ops":[["set",["seen"],{}]],"note":null},{"line":4,"ops":[["set",["i"],0]],"note":null},{"line":5,"ops":[["set",["j"],1]],"note":null},{"line":6,"ops":[["set",["k"],2]],"note":null},{"line":7,"ops":[],"note":"which is the whole cost: this is O(n^3) where the sweep is O(n^2)."},{"line":6